      "id": "42b3d5f2aa29445790a28"
    },
    {
      "text": "\n#### How Spark Fits into the Big Data Ecosystem\n\n- Apache Spark is an open source framework that provides methods to process data in parallel\n- ",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "0203ee700f374e028267f"
    },
    {
      "text": "\n- Spark’s ability to leverage lazy evaluation within memory computations makes it\nparticularly unique\n\n- Apache Spark is an open source framework that provides methods to process data in parallel that are\ngeneralizable; \n\n- the same high-level Spark functions can be used to perform disparate data processing\ntasks on data of different sizes and structures.\n\n-  On its own, Spark is not a data storage solution; \n\n- it performs computations on Spark JVMs (Java Virtual Machines) that last only for the duration of a\nSpark application. ",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
